EyeNet Vision is AI software that turns regular security cameras into smart cameras — running entirely on a standard PC with no cloud dependency, no expensive GPU servers, and all video kept on-premises. It handles people counting, facial recognition, age/gender detection, and automated actions (alerts, digital signage, access control, attendance logging).

Key highlights:
  ▸ Six products on one platform: Presence (attendance), Signage (smart screens), Vradar (alert rules engine), Gate (entrance monitoring), Sentinel (VIP bodyguard wearables/drones), Matrix (multi-site dashboard)
  ▸ 5 of 6 products beta-ready today, working prototype delivered within 6 months (July 2024)
  ▸ Two distribution partners signed: TMA and NewGen Group, both pursuing early-stage enterprise & maritime leads
  ▸ Deloitte EMEA Cyber Security Committee presentation tentatively scheduled for September 2026; LG International identified as a high-potential lead
  ▸ Raising $2.5M Seed (Q3-Q4 2026) → $5-7M Series A → target ~$1M revenue (2027) → ~$26M (2029) → $500M-$1B exit by 2030-2031
  ▸ Differentiators: privacy-first (on-prem, works offline), runs on any standard PC with 16 GB RAM, infinitely scalable microservices architecture, 80-85% gross margins
  ▸ Target markets: retail chains, schools/universities, security companies, commercial buildings/airports, shipping/maritime fleets, government/law enforcement